1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,870
Episode 21: Betrayal Aboard the Burning Ship

2
00:00:06,070 --> 00:00:08,971
When the armada of hundreds of flower boats led by the flagship 'Breeze Wing'
crossed the treacherous ocean swells to reach the southwestern coast of the mainland.

3
00:00:09,071 --> 00:00:11,840
What welcomed the companions was not fluttering banners of celebration, but the
suffocating stench of burning pitch and towering pillars of blackened smoke.

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,981
The timber wharves of Seven Bridges Haven, once a tranquil maritime
sanctuary connecting the northern tundra with the eastern seas.

5
00:00:15,081 --> 00:00:17,810
Had been reduced to smoldering ash, while receding tides dragged
fractured spars and scorched decking across the mudflats.

6
00:00:18,010 --> 00:00:20,459
In this desolate graveyard where
not even a solitary gull cried,

7
00:00:20,559 --> 00:00:23,780
only the bitter reek of scorched cedar bore
testimony to the scale of the atrocity.

8
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:26,760
Rusted harbor chains lay snapped amidst
the tidal mud, and the timber warehouses

9
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,750
along the shoreline stood as skeletal frames
vomiting black soot into the gray sky.

10
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:32,936
Gripping the helm, Rondol
surveyed the ruined piers,

11
00:00:33,036 --> 00:00:35,720
his broad fists trembling
with suppressed rage.

12
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:38,755
[Rondol] "Merciless curs... To trap the fleeing populace, they incinerated
civilian transports and fishing cutters without distinction. A decade ago,

13
00:00:38,855 --> 00:00:41,690
this haven bustled with grain barges and silk merchants from every corner
of the world, yet the madness of those blinded by power knows no boundary."

14
00:00:41,890 --> 00:00:44,806
Bracing his unadorned iron shield, Kadan
leaped first onto the wet mudflats,

15
00:00:44,906 --> 00:00:47,660
his leather boots crunching through
crushed seashells and charcoal dust.

16
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:50,911
[Kadan] "Lucian's imperial vanguard has fortified the
coastline and initiated a brutal scorched-earth campaign.

17
00:00:51,011 --> 00:00:53,630
The fires were set less than half a sunrise ago.
We must search for survivors amidst the ruins."

18
00:00:53,830 --> 00:00:56,954
Raising her Jade Staff to
gather the coastal winds,

19
00:00:57,054 --> 00:00:59,600
Cilia knit her brow in deep concentration.

20
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,348
[Celia] "Beneath the western sea cliffs
near the salt cellar, I sense the faint,

21
00:01:02,448 --> 00:01:05,570
labored breathing of living souls. But lethal mana
snares are woven densely across the approach."

22
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:08,767
Weaving through heaps of sodden ash and charred timber ribs, the
companions advanced cautiously toward the western cliff face.

23
00:01:08,867 --> 00:01:11,540
There lay the canted keel of a massive, burned hospital
barge, dark bloodstains smeared along the fractured hull.

24
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:14,490
Medicine chests and linen bandages lay trampled into the muck, and
upon a broken tea bowl rested the faint, weathered cross-crest of the

25
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:17,510
Arcane Holy Knights. It had been a sanctuary of mercy established decades
ago by Master Aleksandar and Uncle Balian to relieve northern famines.

26
00:01:17,710 --> 00:01:21,007
Smoothing the scarlet ribbon
bound to his silver dagger,

27
00:01:21,107 --> 00:01:23,480
Kadan spoke in a hushed, reverent murmur.

28
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:26,619
[Kadan] "This was the charitable clinic
established by Uncle Balian and the Holy Knights.

29
00:01:26,719 --> 00:01:29,450
A haven that healed impoverished fishermen
and orphans... incinerated into cinder."

30
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:32,593
Just then, a weathered trapdoor at the base of the granite
cliff creaked open, and a white-haired elder brandishing

31
00:01:32,693 --> 00:01:35,420
a broken stone pestle peeked out with trembling wariness.
It was Ordo, the elderly apothecary of the haven.

32
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:39,040
Beholding the sacred cross-crest
upon Kadan's iron shield,

33
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,390
Ordo broke into racking sobs of relief.

34
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:44,425
[Harbor Elder] "Praise be to the heavens! The sacred shield of the Holy
Knights has returned! Lucian's Crimson Wolf vanguard put the harbor to

35
00:01:44,525 --> 00:01:47,360
the torch and dragged our able-bodied youths to the labor mines, but I
managed to conceal twenty orphaned children beneath these salt vaults!"

36
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:50,104
[Ignis] Stepping forward, Ignis took the old man's
trembling hands, bowing his head in solemn remorse.

37
00:01:50,204 --> 00:01:53,330
"Forgive our tardy arrival, elder. For the atrocities committed
by the imperial host, I offer my life in earnest atonement."

38
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:56,112
[Celia] Cilia lifted a broken ceramic herb
jar, tears glittering upon her lashes.

39
00:01:56,212 --> 00:01:59,300
"To set fire to a sanctuary dedicated solely to
mercy and healing is an unforgivable sacrilege."

40
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:02,297
Descending into the salt cellar, the
companions beheld twenty orphaned refugee

41
00:02:02,397 --> 00:02:05,270
children and wounded fishermen huddled
together amidst sacks of coarse sea salt.

42
00:02:05,470 --> 00:02:08,191
Caked in grime and starving after days without
rations, the children shivered, while injured mariners

43
00:02:08,291 --> 00:02:11,240
clutched gangrenous limbs in silent agony. The damp
subterranean chill froze the little ones' bare feet blue.

44
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:13,728
Without a second thought, Cilia
knelt upon the damp stone,

45
00:02:13,828 --> 00:02:17,210
extracting soothing restorative powders from
her satchel to dress their lacerations.

46
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:20,245
[Celia] "Do not fear. You are
safe now. This is the soothing

47
00:02:20,345 --> 00:02:23,180
balm of mountain herbs brought
from Whispering Wind Island."

48
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:26,322
As gentle teal mana radiated from
Cilia's staff, stroking the children's

49
00:02:26,422 --> 00:02:29,150
fevered brows, their rasping breath
smoothed into peaceful cadence.

50
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:32,687
Kadan drew loaves of barley bread
and dried venison from his pack,

51
00:02:32,787 --> 00:02:35,120
placing them into the
children's fragile hands.

52
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,866
[Kadan] "Eat slowly and take
heart. Beyond these shores,

53
00:02:37,966 --> 00:02:41,090
hundreds of festive flower boats
are waiting to bear you to safety."

54
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:43,920
[Refugee Child] A small girl touched Kadan's
battered iron shield with her tiny fingers,

55
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:47,060
weeping softly. "Mister knight... The men in armor
set fire to our home... Where has my mother gone?"

56
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:49,950
Caressing the girl's hair
with tender gentleness,

57
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:53,030
Kadan mastered the blazing
fury surging in his breast.

58
00:02:53,230 --> 00:02:56,157
[Kadan] "I will find your mother,
little one. And those who crushed

59
00:02:56,257 --> 00:02:59,000
your hearth shall answer for
every drop of sorrow they caused."

60
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:02,243
[Ignis] Offering his canteen of honeyed water to the injured
elders, Ignis spoke with earnest depth. "Moisten your throats.

61
00:03:02,343 --> 00:03:04,970
I swear upon my life to hold this battle line so the
hunting hounds of the court can never harm you again."

62
00:03:05,170 --> 00:03:08,169
In that tender moment, the sharp crunch of armored boots
and the rhythmic creak of cocked crossbows echoed outside.

63
00:03:08,269 --> 00:03:10,940
Thirty elite inquisitors of Lucian's guard, alerted
by the smoke, had cordoned off the cellar entrance.

64
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:13,960
[Inquisitor Captain] Kicking down the outer door,
the inquisition commander sneered in cruel triumph.

65
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:16,910
"So the vermin survived beneath the stones! Exterminate
the traitors and feed their bones to the sea!"

66
00:03:17,110 --> 00:03:19,856
Without hesitation, Kadan charged through
the threshold, raising his iron shield.

67
00:03:19,956 --> 00:03:22,880
A volley of poisoned bolts shattered against
the curved surface with deafening clangs.

68
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:25,594
[Kadan] "Not a single foot shall approach these children!"
Channeling star-breathing, Kadan spun his shield,

69
00:03:25,694 --> 00:03:28,850
snapping spearheads and shattering the vanguard's formation. Ignis
charged beside him, his iron weapon wreathed in roaring white fire.

70
00:03:29,050 --> 00:03:31,158
The sanctified heat incinerated
the assassins' plate armor,

71
00:03:31,258 --> 00:03:34,820
driving them headlong into the muck, while Cilia's
blinding sandstorm stripped away their vision.

72
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:37,855
Sprawling in the mud, the
inquisition commander hurled

73
00:03:37,955 --> 00:03:40,790
away his shattered helmet,
shrieking in venomous rage.

74
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:43,872
[Inquisitor Captain] "Ignis! Have you truly
renounced the grace of the throne to become a lackey

75
00:03:43,972 --> 00:03:46,760
for northern rebels! Minister Lucian has placed
the empire's greatest bounty upon your head!"

76
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:49,774
[Ignis] Planting his weapon into the earth, Ignis glared down with frigid
disdain. "Lucian's 'grace' is merely a sandcastle built on the blood

77
00:03:49,874 --> 00:03:52,730
of the innocent. Return and tell him: the shield of the Holy Knights and
the flame of redemption will soon arrive to shatter his gilded throne!"

78
00:03:52,930 --> 00:03:58,700
With the threat vanquished, tranquil
surf returned to the shore.

79
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:01,628
Kadan and Ignis escorted the refugees
safely onto the flower boats,

80
00:04:01,728 --> 00:04:04,670
where Rondol's crew served steaming
carp soup to the shivering children.

81
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:07,846
Beyond the western horizon, the rose-gold dusk cast
long, dramatic shadows across the ruined harbor.

82
00:04:07,946 --> 00:04:10,640
From the decks of the flower boats drifted the
tender, solemn melodies of seafarers' hymns.

83
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,249
[Celia] Touching the scorched stone of the
lighthouse, Cilia spoke with solemn resolve.

84
00:04:13,349 --> 00:04:16,610
"The entire continent groans beneath Lucian's reign of
terror. The road ahead will test every fiber of our spirits."

85
00:04:16,810 --> 00:04:19,555
[Ignis] Ignis clenched his fists with unyielding conviction.
"They burned timber and stone, but they could never

86
00:04:19,655 --> 00:04:22,580
incinerate the hope of the people. At every crossroads toward
the capital, we will deliver the suffering from despair."

87
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:25,984
Gazing toward the distant
western mountain passes,

88
00:04:26,084 --> 00:04:28,550
Kadan tightened his grip on his dagger.

89
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:31,627
[Kadan] "This is the realm Master Aleksandar and Uncle
Balian bled to protect. Even in the ashes of despair,

90
00:04:31,727 --> 00:04:34,520
we have defended the warmth of living souls. Now we
raise our shields and walk that road until the dawn."

91
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,555
Under the dying light of dusk, the three youths sealed their
unbreakable oath, taking their first bold strides into the heart

92
00:04:37,655 --> 00:04:40,490
of the troubled continent. Beyond the cold night fog, the rugged
peaks of Mount Dragonhorn silently watched over their march.

93
00:04:40,690 --> 00:04:46,460
